{# THE FILES HUB — /files.

   STATIC TWIN of the settled design's files/index.html. Same page furniture,
   same copy; the sample area's twenty-three files become the registry's own.

   The widget grid is the HOST's framework (.w-grid / .w-cell / .w-span-N), so a
   person arranges this surface exactly as they arrange departments or team. The
   widgets themselves live in _w_<id>.html.twig and are rendered by BOTH this
   screen and the library, so a preview can never drift from the real thing.

   THERE IS NO UPLOAD CONTROL ON THIS PAGE, and that is a rule rather than an
   omission: a file arrives by being attached to a record, on that record's own
   page, and it carries that record's name for the rest of its life. #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiStorage/base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Files{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}<a href="/">uhifadhi</a> / files{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}Files{% endblock %}

{# ONE LINE. The strip says which tab you are on, and the argument behind the
   page belongs in this comment rather than on the screen: a file is never
   loose on this platform — it is an observation's photograph, an incident's
   evidence, and one day a permit's document. This hub is the one place all of
   them can be read at once, but it is not a shelf you upload onto. #}
{% block shell_page_subtitle %}Every photograph, document and track, with the record it belongs to.{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_actions %}
    <a class="tgl w-act" href="{{ settingsUrl }}">{{ ux_icon('storage:settings') }} Where files go</a>
    <a class="tgl w-act" href="{{ libraryUrl }}">{{ ux_icon('shell:layout-grid') }} Widget library</a>
{% endblock %}

{% block storage_page %}
{% set widgetContext = {
    filter: filter,
    files: files,
    total: total,
    counts: counts,
    modules: modules,
    areas: areas,
    days: days,
    kinds: kinds,
    facets: facets,
    byOwner: byOwner,
    byDay: byDay,
    byKind: byKind,
    bySpace: bySpace,
    byArea: byArea,
    arrivals: arrivals,
    recent: recent,
    biggest: biggest,
    waiting: waiting,
    places: places,
    thumbnailLongEdge: thumbnailLongEdge,
    now: now,
} %}



{# FRAGMENTS, NOT AN ESSAY. What a reader has to know to use this page is
   four facts; the argument behind them is in the comment above. #}
<div class="f-say">{{ ux_icon('shell:info') }}<div><b>Every file belongs to a record.</b> Browse, find, check, tidy &mdash; <b>never upload</b>. A file arrives by being attached to a record. Originals sit outside the website and are handed over only after a permission check.</div></div>

{# The person's own resolved layout, in their own order, with the widgets they
   switched off simply absent. #}
<div class="w-grid" data-surface="files">
    {% for widget in widgets|filter(w => w.on) %}
        <div class="w-cell w-span-{{ widget.cols }}" data-widget-id="{{ widget.id }}" data-widget-cols="{{ widget.cols }}">
            <div class="w-inner">
                {{ include('@UhifadhiStorage/files/_w_' ~ widget.id ~ '.html.twig', widgetContext, with_context: false) }}
            </div>
        </div>
    {% endfor %}
</div>

<h2 class="zone">What the hub knows that a module page does not</h2>
<div class="grid g2">
    <div class="c">
        <span class="tab">How a file is kept</span>
        <div class="rln"><span>Where an original lives</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">outside the web root, always</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>How it is reached</span><span class="mono acc" style="font-size:11px">a request the app answers after a permission check</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>What browsing costs</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">one ~{{ thumbnailLongEdge }}px picture per file</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>Small pictures per file</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">exactly one &mdash; never a set of sizes</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>What decides the type</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">detection, never the file&rsquo;s name</span></div>
        <div class="use" style="margin-bottom:0">A refusal is a <b>not found</b>, never a <b>not allowed</b> &mdash; being
        told you may not see something confirms it exists, and evidence must not confirm itself to a stranger.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="c">
        <span class="tab">Who owns what</span>
        <p class="use" style="margin-top:2px">The hub <b>browses and manages</b>; it never overrules. Whether a file may be removed is the <b>owning record&rsquo;s</b> answer. Open any file and it says which, in the module&rsquo;s own words.</p>
        {% for module in modules %}
            <div class="rln"><span>{{ module.label }}</span><span class="f-note">{{ module.attachesTo }}</span></div>
        {% else %}
            <div class="rln"><span>Modules holding files</span><span class="f-note">none installed yet</span></div>
        {% endfor %}
        <div class="rln"><span>Who may see a file</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">whoever may see its record</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>Who may remove one</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">whoever the record says</span></div>
        <div class="use" style="margin-bottom:0">A module puts its files here by shipping a file source; nothing on this
        page has to know what an observation or an incident is, and it does not.</div>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
